\title{pprof: Modeling, Standardization and Testing for Provider Profiling}
\description{
pprof fits risk-adjusted models with an effect for each provider (a hospital, a dialysis
facility, a transplant center, a school) and profiles the providers: it tests each
provider's effect and flags the providers whose outcomes are higher or lower than
expected, computes indirectly and directly standardized measures with their intervals,
and draws funnel, caterpillar, flag, and volume plots.
}
\section{Fitting}{

For binary outcomes, \code{\link[=fit_logistic_fe]{fit_logistic_fe()}} fits a fixed effect for each provider with the
SerBIN or BAN algorithm, \code{\link[=fit_logistic_firth]{fit_logistic_firth()}} adds Firth's bias-reducing penalty,
\code{\link[=fit_logistic_re]{fit_logistic_re()}} fits random effects, and \code{\link[=fit_logistic_cre]{fit_logistic_cre()}} correlated random
effects. For continuous outcomes, \code{\link[=fit_linear_fe]{fit_linear_fe()}}, \code{\link[=fit_linear_re]{fit_linear_re()}}, and
\code{\link[=fit_linear_cre]{fit_linear_cre()}} fit the corresponding linear models. Every fit takes a formula, a data
frame, and the name of the provider column.
}

\section{Profiling providers}{

\code{\link[=test_providers]{test_providers()}} tests and flags providers, \code{\link[=standardize_providers]{standardize_providers()}} computes
standardized measures with optional intervals, \code{\link[=provider_effects]{provider_effects()}} gives the provider
effects with optional intervals, \code{\link[=funnel_limits]{funnel_limits()}} computes the control limits of a
funnel plot, and \code{\link[=profile_providers]{profile_providers()}} runs all of these at once. For the covariates,
\link[=summary.pprof_model]{summary()}, \link[=confint.pprof_model]{confint()}, and
\code{\link[=test_coefficients]{test_coefficients()}} give tests and intervals of the coefficients.
}

\section{Plots}{

\code{\link[=plot_funnel]{plot_funnel()}}, \code{\link[=plot_caterpillar]{plot_caterpillar()}}, \code{\link[=plot_flags]{plot_flags()}}, and \code{\link[=plot_volume]{plot_volume()}} draw the
results with ggplot2 and return the plot.
}

